Z||000000||Fformula88||01-22-2001||07:36 PM||||I just got back from the salvage yard with a TON of stuff I will be using to rebuild the 87 SC I cracked up a couple weeks ago.  I picket up the front fascia, rear fascia, both impact bars, the hood and front fenders, pass side quarter panel, rear side markers and front turn signals, the headlights, all brackets and motors (and they work!!) drivers side door hinges, the pass side quarter window, center console (no peeling!) wiper motor, and a coffee can full of nuts, bolts and stuff for $600!  It was also an 87 SC so it all matches!  I cannot wait to start reassemblying it all!  Unfortunately there really isn't anything else left on the car that is useable.  The drivetrain has been ripped out and the interior was left exposed to the winter snow.  It was a gold coupe with 117K miles upon death, but at least its saving ours.  Wish me luck!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">     <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
